 ```
 
+### decamelizeKeys(object, options?)
+
+Decamelize each own enumerable string key of a plain object. Returns a new object; values are untouched and nested objects are not traversed. If multiple keys decamelize to the same key, the last one wins. Throws a `TypeError` for non-plain objects.
+
+The `options` are passed through to `decamelize`.
+
+```js
+import {decamelizeKeys} from 'decamelize';
+
+decamelizeKeys({unicornRainbow: 1, fooBar: {bazQux: 2}}, {separator: '-'});
+//=> {'unicorn-rainbow': 1, 'foo-bar': {bazQux: 2}}
+```
+
